Vite 6/7 SPA (React, Vue or Svelte): the banner markup sits in index.html next to the app root (the framework never touches it), consent.js lives in `public/` so Vite copies it unchanged to the site root, and it loads as a CLASSIC script (`defer`, not `type="module"`). `vite-ignore` tells Vite not to process that tag. There is no nonce on a static host: scripts/csp-hashes.mjs (headers recipe) adds the SRI hash to the tag and to the CSP, and 'strict-dynamic' trusts the Google tag this script creates, so never host-allow Google in script-src. The CSS is imported from the entry so it is bundled and hashed. List `consent` under essentialCookies and set consent.banner.acceptLabel/rejectLabel/reopenLabel to the three labels. Build with CSP_CONNECT_EXTRA="https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://www.googletagmanager.com" CSP_IMG_EXTRA="https://www.google-analytics.com" (beacons only).
