A Vite SPA is served as static files, so there is no per-request nonce: a post-build script hashes every inline script, adds SRI `integrity` to the same-origin entry scripts and writes `_headers` into dist (Netlify and Cloudflare Pages read it; Vercel: build with HOST=vercel and merge the written `vercel.headers.json` "headers" array into vercel.json). Do not also keep a `public/_headers` (the build output overwrites it). Vite's hashed files in `/assets/` (build.assetsDir default `assets`) get `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable`; HTML keeps the hosts' default `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`. `build.modulePreload: false` because Vite's CSP support puts a nonce on `<link rel=modulepreload>` and a static host has none, and an un-nonced preload link can be blocked under 'strict-dynamic'; `assetsInlineLimit: 0` avoids `data:` fonts. Run the script last and do not minify or inject into HTML on the host afterwards. Cloudflare Pages caps a `_headers` line at 2,000 characters (the script refuses longer). Dev server is unaffected.
