robots.txt, sitemap.xml and the non-production noindex header are generated AFTER `vite build`, from the build environment: the script reads `process.env.DEPLOY_ENV` and `SITE_URL` (Node). Do NOT use `import.meta.env` for this: Vite inlines env into the client bundle at build time and only exposes `VITE_`-prefixed variables, and the files are not part of the bundle. Set DEPLOY_ENV=production only on the production deploy (Netlify/Cloudflare previews and branch builds must not be `production`) and SITE_URL=https://example.com. The sitemap is built from the prerendered pages (the `routes` list in vite.config.ts is the single source of truth): every page that is not noindex and not an error page, using its `<link rel="canonical">` as the URL; render that tag per route in the component (`<link rel="canonical" href="https://example.com/about/" />`, hoisted by React 19) with one trailing-slash policy. Delete any hand-written public/robots.txt and public/sitemap.xml. Edit PRIVATE to your real app/API paths (never /assets/ or other CSS/JS folders). Run it after csp-hashes.mjs (which writes X-Robots-Tag into `_headers` for non-production builds).
